@page "/get-help-now"
@model GetHelpNowModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Get help now";
}

@* WI-103: helplines + crisis resources, one click from every page
   (sitemap.md). Plain language, calm framing — no alarm styling. *@

<h1>Get help now</h1>
<p>
    You do not have to figure this out alone. The people below are free to
    call, and they help patients and families every day.
</p>

<h2>If you might hurt yourself</h2>
<p>
    Call or text <strong>988</strong> any time, day or night. It is the
    Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline. The call is free and private.
</p>
<p>
    If you would rather text, send the word <strong>HOME</strong> to
    <strong>741741</strong>. A trained person from the Crisis Text Line will
    text back.
</p>
<p>
    <a class="button" href="tel:988">Call 988</a>
    <a class="button" href="sms:741741?body=HOME">Text HOME to 741741</a>
</p>
<p>If someone is in danger right now, call <strong>911</strong>.</p>

<h2>If you want to talk about a brain tumor</h2>
<p>
    The American Brain Tumor Association CareLine is free. The people who
    answer know brain tumors. They can explain terms, help you find support
    groups, and point you to resources near you.
</p>
<p>
    <a class="button" href="tel:8008862282">Call the CareLine: 800-886-2282</a>
</p>
<p>
    The National Cancer Institute also answers questions about any cancer,
    in English and Spanish (1-800-4-CANCER).
</p>
<p>
    <a class="button" href="tel:8004226237">Call the NCI: 800-422-6237</a>
</p>

<h2>If you are caring for someone</h2>
<p>
    Caregivers need support too. CancerCare has social workers who talk with
    caregivers for free.
</p>
<p>
    <a class="button" href="tel:8008134673">Call CancerCare: 800-813-4673</a>
</p>
